  "tldr": [
    "Multi-agent development tooling explodes: Karpathy's agent command center vision, Claude Code's multi-agent PR review, watcher scripts for looping agents, and LangGraph's one-command deployment all point to agents-managing-agents as the new default.",
    "Agentic security and evals become acquisition targets: OpenAI buying Promptfoo signals that testing, red-teaming, and evaluating autonomous agents is now critical infrastructure worth buying, not building.",
    "Enterprise guardrails arrive: Amazon requiring senior engineer sign-off on AI code and a court blocking Perplexity's shopping agents mark the first formal governance boundaries around autonomous AI in production.",
    "The agent-to-agent economy is forming: Meta acquiring an agent social network, agent-to-agent communication protocols gaining traction, and Anthropic launching a dedicated AI governance institute all signal the ecosystem is preparing for agents that interact with each other, not just humans.",
    "Google plays the integration moat game: While everyone else builds new agent tools, Google is deeply embedding Gemini into Workspace with product-specific tuning — betting that AI woven into existing workflows beats standalone agent products."
  ],
